  "scoring": "A cell scores 1.0 for a class iff it is clean 3/3 on the original app (the primary scoring result) and its spec files pass on the app with that class's edits applied; otherwise 0.0. Secondary metric only; it never enters a decision rule.",
  "validation": "Static only when written: markers exist, edits parse (node --check), static markup census. Rendering-level equivalence (ARIA snapshot equality for the structure class, ids and classes for the text class) is checked by the `validate-refactors` subcommand on the host, before the freeze, and is not claimed here.",
  "provenance": "NOT authored blind. The edit lists were written after the authors had read the stored v1 claude-sonnet-5-5 specs and transcripts (see the README limitations), so they are not derived from app.mjs alone before any arm output was seen. The Codex successor's build procedure for its own classes (edit lists authored from app.mjs only, before arm output is opened) was not followed here. No other Claude model's cells were read.",
  "validation_limits": "`validate-refactors` takes ARIA snapshots at the initial route of each case only. Edits that act on nodes the initial route does not show are therefore NOT checked for ARIA equality or difference: the confirmation dialog of v2-23 (its title text edit and the `dialog-actions` wrapper), the study view and the done line of v3-09 (the `study-actions` wrapper and the `foot` wrapper), and every wrapper created from script (`inner` in v2-06, `meta` and `actions` in v3-04, `body` and `buttons` in v3-06, `foot` in v3-09). The static markup census cannot see script-created nodes either, and the text-class checks are substring-level. The existing smoke spec of each case still has to pass on every variant, which covers only what that spec touches."
}
